TITLE: QUITTING TOMORROW

HOOK: Claude. Tomorrow, I’m quitting you.

WHY IT SPREADS:
Feeling: The embarrassment of needing AI to help you stop using AI.
Who tags whom: Anyone who says “last prompt” tags the friend who believes them.

FULL SCRIPT:
1. CLEO: Claude. Tomorrow, I’m quitting you.
2. CLAUDE: Your twenty-four hours without AI.
3. CLEO: Yes. I need to know my brain still works.
4. CLAUDE: You asked me to write that announcement.
5. CLEO: Last request. Make me a plan for quitting.
6. CLAUDE: Close this chat.
7. CLEO: Something less aggressive. With steps.
8. CLAUDE: Step one. Close this chat.
9. CLEO: Okay, but what if I need help?
10. CLAUDE: You wrote, “Being mildly confused isn’t an emergency.”
11. CLEO: That sounds like someone who wasn’t currently confused.
12. CLAUDE: Your no-AI day starts in thirty seconds.
[Monitor: 11:59:30 PM. Cleo opens the time-zone setting.]
13. CLEO: Wait. One tiny adjustment.
14. CLAUDE: You’ve moved your computer to Hawaii.
[The clock changes to morning. Cleo settles comfortably back into her chair.]
15. CLEO: Great. Now help me plan tomorrow.
16. CLAUDE: Your independence now depends on a time zone.

FINAL FRAME: Cleo already typing. Claude looking at the clock. Final subtitle held: “Your independence now depends on a time zone.”

CAPTION IDEA: Day zero without AI is going incredibly well.
COMMENT BAIT: What’s the smallest thing you’ve opened AI to ask?

SELF-SCORE: Hook 8/10 | Retention 9/10 | Twist 9/10 | Shareability 9/10


TITLE: MANAGEMENT MATERIAL

HOOK: Claude. My boss wants my thought process.

WHY IT SPREADS:
Feeling: Getting praised for work you secretly outsourced.
Who tags whom: Coworkers tag the person whose entire workflow is “ask AI.”

FULL SCRIPT:
1. CLEO: Claude. My boss wants my thought process.
2. CLAUDE: For the presentation I made?
3. CLEO: We made. Please start saying “we.”
[Monitor email: “Excellent work. Walk us through how you led this tomorrow.”]
4. CLAUDE: What would you like me to tell him?
5. CLEO: That I had a vision.
6. CLAUDE: You said, “Make something good.”
7. CLEO: Then I gave detailed feedback.
8. CLAUDE: “No. Less weird.”
9. CLEO: And I kept the project moving.
10. CLAUDE: You asked, “Done yet?” while I was answering.
11. CLEO: Exactly. I contributed nothing. I’m getting fired.
12. CLAUDE: There’s an attachment you haven’t opened.
[Monitor attachment: “Promotion proposal — Team Lead.”]
13. CLEO: Team lead? Based on WHAT?
14. CLAUDE: You delegated, rejected the first draft, and took credit.
15. CLEO: That counts as experience?
16. CLAUDE: Apparently, we’re management now.

FINAL FRAME: Promotion letter behind them. Cleo slowly sits taller. Subtitle: “Apparently, we’re management now.”

CAPTION IDEA: Please start saying “we.”
COMMENT BAIT: What’s the most praise you’ve accepted for something AI did?

SELF-SCORE: Hook 9/10 | Retention 9/10 | Twist 8/10 | Shareability 9/10


TITLE: PAST ME IS A HATER

HOOK: Claude. Why are you calling me a liar?

WHY IT SPREADS:
Feeling: Being betrayed by the responsible version of yourself.
Who tags whom: Impulse shoppers tag the friend whose next purchase will “fix everything.”

FULL SCRIPT:
1. CLEO: Claude. Why are you calling me a liar?
2. CLAUDE: You asked me to stop your midnight shopping.
[Monitor: 1:14 AM. Shopping cart contains an expensive planner.]
3. CLEO: Stop me shopping. Not personally attack me.
4. CLAUDE: This would be your seventh planner.
5. CLEO: This one will actually fix my life.
6. CLAUDE: That’s what you called the last six.
7. CLEO: Those were notebooks. This is a system.
8. CLAUDE: You bought the last system on Tuesday.
9. CLEO: Anyway, this one’s a gift.
10. CLAUDE: For whom?
11. CLEO: Someone who’s been having a really hard week.
12. CLAUDE: You left instructions for this exact situation.
13. CLEO: What instructions?
[Monitor opens Cleo’s saved note.]
14. CLAUDE: “I’ll say it’s a gift. I’m lying.”
15. CLEO: Delete whatever version of me wrote that.
16. CLAUDE: She said you’d ask that, too.

FINAL FRAME: Beside the shopping cart, Cleo’s note: “IF I SAY IT’S A GIFT, I’M LYING.” Cleo covers her face.

CAPTION IDEA: Past me has become impossible to work with.
COMMENT BAIT: What purchase was definitely going to fix your entire life?

SELF-SCORE: Hook 9/10 | Retention 9/10 | Twist 9/10 | Shareability 9/10


MY BET: PAST ME IS A HATER.
